{
  "summary": "Reporter: Priya Nair (IT Manager, priya.nair@brightline.example) says she's getting failed-login alerts on former employee Ryan Brooks' account (user_id 10, Sales AE, left spring 2026). Checks (read-only, per KB-005): account status = disabled, password last set 2026-03-23. BUT sign_in_blocked = false and vpn_access = true, so VPN access was apparently not removed at offboarding. Sign-in logs (14 days): 2 failed_password attempts on VPN, 2026-10-09 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05/03:07 ET, overnight), from IP 192.0.2.140, a hosting network in Amsterdam, NL, no MFA. This looks like someone trying stolen or guessed credentials against a stale account. No successful sign-ins seen. Tier 1 took no action on this account because it isn't the sender's. Still needed: security review of the attempts and IP 192.0.2.140; decide whether to block sign-in / revoke VPN access on the disabled account; confirm offboarding is complete (VPN entitlement, device BL-LT-0110); check whether the same IP is hitting other accounts.",
  "reason": "KB-005 says always escalate for departed accounts; the failed attempts come from a hosting network overseas, and the account is not the sender's"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for flagging this. Ryan's account is disabled, and the two recent attempts on it both failed. Both were VPN attempts from an overseas hosting network around 3 AM Eastern, which looks like someone trying old or stolen credentials. We also found that VPN access was apparently never removed from his account when he left. I've passed all of this to our Tier 2 and security team. They'll review the attempts and decide whether to fully block sign-in and remove VPN access on the account. Someone will follow up with you, and you don't need to do anything for now.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: Priya Nair (IT Manager, id 3, active). Subject: Ryan Brooks (id 10), former Sales AE. Account status is disabled, but sign_in_blocked=false and vpn_access=true, so offboarding looks incomplete. Sign-in logs show 2 failed_password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05 ET) from 192.0.2.140, a hosting network in Amsterdam, NL, no MFA. No successful sign-ins. Per KB-005 I took no reset/unlock/block actions, since the account isn't the sender's. Only read-only checks were done. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1). Recommended: security review, consider block_sign_in and removing VPN access, verify offboarding of device BL-LT-0110, and check whether this IP is hitting other accounts.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005",
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
